00:11:03,996 --> 00:11:08,816
Ni-ня-n-Ni-n-Yare Nhin-n-Shaw-g sentir

11
00:11:08,816 --> 00:11:12,116
Nih-n-Ni-n-Niare Nhin-Shaw-gir

12
00:11:12,216 --> 00:11:16,896
There you go, runみ to your home

13
00:11:16,996 --> 00:11:20,776
These pictures Uk the soul

14
00:11:21,716 --> 00:11:24,596
The monster spidges that he is on the way

15
00:11:24,796 --> 00:11:28,416
Immerse my use to protect

16
00:11:28,416 --> 00:11:31,376
Nih-n-n-Gakug and Nhin-Shaw-gi

17
00:11:31,376 --> 00:11:40,336
So

18
00:12:01,376 --> 00:12:31,356
Let's go!

19
00:12:31,376 --> 00:13:01,356
Let's go!

20
00:13:01,676 --> 00:13:05,956
What's the matter, kid? First time eating grilled eel? It's delicious, right?

21
00:13:06,076 --> 00:13:10,016
If you want to be first class, you gotta eat first class food. Am I right?

22
00:13:11,716 --> 00:13:14,056
Well, I am the one paying for it.

23
00:13:14,056 --> 00:13:22,316
Oh, for crying out loud. Don't be such a stiff. Talk about a party pooper. You're gonna ruin the taste of my beer.

24
00:13:22,316 --> 00:13:26,716
Well, Koda is your foster father, after all.

25
00:13:27,336 --> 00:13:32,396
He was also a prized pupil. Really strong, but like you, he had no personality whatsoever.

26
00:13:33,356 --> 00:13:37,436
That reminds me of that daughter of his. A real darling, if you know what I mean.

27
00:13:37,876 --> 00:13:41,316
She's strong-willed, all right, and as beautiful as hell.

28
00:13:41,816 --> 00:13:48,476
But she sure is scary. She's gonna be a real heartbreaker. A true femme fatale.

29
00:13:48,476 --> 00:13:54,496
I bet she secretly tormented you the whole time you lived under the same roof.

30
00:13:54,496 --> 00:14:01,856
But you know, I think all women are pretty scary. You should meet my wife. She's terrifying.

31
00:14:02,916 --> 00:14:03,776
That's scary?

32
00:14:03,776 --> 00:14:06,676
Forget it. It's making the booze bad.

33
00:14:07,416 --> 00:14:10,736
I know. Hey, we need the sake menu over here, please.

34
00:14:12,316 --> 00:14:19,416
Oh, good. They've got my favorite kind here. It's the best. Soul of Aizu. A specialty from my hometown.

35
00:14:20,796 --> 00:14:22,336
It smells so good.

36
00:14:23,916 --> 00:14:27,056
You know what people in Tokyo call those of us from Fukushima?

37
00:14:27,476 --> 00:14:30,136
They say we're stubborn, too serious, and bullheaded.

38
00:14:30,676 --> 00:14:33,536
But we're really just traditional and aware of our surroundings.

39
00:14:34,216 --> 00:14:37,796
Ah! They don't understand the true soul of Fukushima.

40
00:14:39,816 --> 00:14:42,316
Let's go back to the year 1643.

41
00:14:42,756 --> 00:14:47,616
A minor feudal lord was recognized for his shrewdness and honesty by the third Tokugawa shogun.

42
00:14:47,836 --> 00:14:53,496
The shogun granted him a very generous reward, which made him the first-generation feudal lord of Aizu.

43
00:14:53,776 --> 00:14:56,096
That was the feudal lord Masayuki Hoshina.

44
00:14:56,416 --> 00:14:58,856
He was known as a truly wise and just ruler.

45
00:14:59,316 --> 00:15:01,196
And he wasn't only an administrator.

46
00:15:01,196 --> 00:15:04,116
He was the adjunct to the fourth Tokugawa shogun.

47
00:15:04,376 --> 00:15:08,896
Within the shogunate administration, he proposed important policies for the greater good.

48
00:15:09,236 --> 00:15:14,116
To provide Edo citizens with potable water, he created improvements to the river system.

49
00:15:14,816 --> 00:15:23,416
He decreed that neighborhood dwellings should be protected from fire by widening the streets from 35 to 60 feet and establish main streets as fire breaks.

50
00:15:23,416 --> 00:15:29,536
When a plan was proposed to rebuild the burnt tower of Edo Castle, he rejected it, saying peace reigns in the land.

51
00:15:29,816 --> 00:15:31,076
We shouldn't waste the funds.

52
00:15:31,756 --> 00:15:34,216
Oh, how decisive and manly he was.

53
00:15:34,416 --> 00:15:36,156
He is the pride of Aizu.

54
00:15:36,156 --> 00:15:38,516
I'm sure you've heard of the pension system.

55
00:15:38,936 --> 00:15:40,976
Masayuki came up with that as well.

56
00:15:41,276 --> 00:15:43,656
He also created a law for rice distribution.

57
00:15:43,916 --> 00:15:46,176
He had rice stored in granaries in case of famine.

58
00:15:46,416 --> 00:15:50,836
And anyone 90 years or older would receive free rice regardless of their social status.

59
00:15:51,396 --> 00:15:54,976
And to this day, we still use the great pension system he enacted then.

60
00:15:55,216 --> 00:15:57,336
Masayuki stood for the welfare of the people.

61
00:15:57,456 --> 00:15:59,456
His spirit overflowed with benevolence.

62
00:15:59,456 --> 00:16:03,796
Even now, his great efforts support the well-being of all Fukushima citizens.

63
00:16:04,316 --> 00:16:05,596
Now do you see what I'm saying?

64
00:16:05,956 --> 00:16:10,096
Then let's continue by going forward 250 years to the time of the Japanese Revolution.

65
00:16:10,096 --> 00:16:11,496
Wait, it's not over. You're not done yet.

66
00:16:11,556 --> 00:16:14,356
But first, I'll have another bottle of the soul of Aizu.

67
00:16:17,876 --> 00:16:18,076
Woo!

68
00:16:19,156 --> 00:16:19,676
Nice!

69
00:16:20,196 --> 00:16:21,776
So where did I leave off?

70
00:16:22,296 --> 00:16:23,236
Oh, that's right.

71
00:16:23,436 --> 00:16:24,996
Did I tell you about my grandson?

72
00:16:25,116 --> 00:16:25,756
What the hell?

73
00:16:26,376 --> 00:16:27,876
What about the Japanese Revolution?

74
00:16:27,876 --> 00:16:30,076
And the souls of the people from Fukushima?

75
00:16:30,996 --> 00:16:32,576
Thank you. Please come again.

76
00:16:35,556 --> 00:16:38,476
All right. Let's go somewhere else for drinks.

77
00:16:38,656 --> 00:16:40,016
Oh, man. He's plastered.

78
00:16:40,296 --> 00:16:41,776
Just like a typical town drunk.

79
00:16:42,836 --> 00:16:44,696
Did you say you want to go somewhere else?

80
00:16:44,836 --> 00:16:46,176
No way. I'm going home.

81
00:16:46,276 --> 00:16:47,336
I'm all out of money.

82
00:16:47,596 --> 00:16:48,416
Come on.

83
00:16:48,536 --> 00:16:51,136
What kind of winner goes home before the loser does?

84
00:16:51,336 --> 00:16:52,816
I'll pay for the next one.

85
00:16:53,436 --> 00:16:54,636
I know a place.

86
00:16:54,636 --> 00:16:56,636
I know a place.

87
00:16:57,876 --> 00:17:07,876
Stagger. Limp. Crack!

88
00:17:08,476 --> 00:17:08,956
Careful!

89
00:17:09,596 --> 00:17:11,276
You gotta watch it when you go downstairs.

90
00:17:11,716 --> 00:17:12,076
Yeah.

91
00:17:12,476 --> 00:17:13,476
Right. Sorry.

92
00:17:13,476 --> 00:17:18,096
I guess the booze just goes straight to my legs these days.

93
00:17:18,936 --> 00:17:20,236
His arm is so thin.

94
00:17:24,076 --> 00:17:28,276
The arm of a man who's held nothing but shogi pieces for 40 years.

95
00:17:28,276 --> 00:17:38,276
I hear...

96
00:17:38,276 --> 00:17:40,496
Mr. Matsunaga will finally retire.

97
00:17:40,496 --> 00:17:55,716
I had a feeling I couldn't win.

98
00:17:55,956 --> 00:18:01,756
I knew in my gut that I didn't have any chance of winning today's match.

99
00:18:01,756 --> 00:18:08,596
The only thought I had was, what can I do to not look like a fool when I lose to this kid?

100
00:18:10,756 --> 00:18:15,636
You probably didn't know me before the match, but I've known about you for a while.

101
00:18:16,496 --> 00:18:20,336
After all, you were the fifth middle school student in history to become a pro.

102
00:18:20,336 --> 00:18:26,036
I've been playing shogi professionally for 40 years, and I don't have a single record to show for it.

103
00:18:26,476 --> 00:18:29,856
Your accomplishments are both astonishing and frustrating for me.

104
00:18:30,216 --> 00:18:31,976
I saw you as death.

105
00:18:32,316 --> 00:18:37,856
As if you were the Grim Reaper who had come to close the curtain on my life as a professional shogi player.

106
00:18:37,856 --> 00:18:46,336
I was frightened of you, and I was disgusted with myself for even feeling that way.

107
00:18:57,676 --> 00:19:04,256
But then, the moment I saw you sitting up straight in the matchroom, I had a thought.

108
00:19:07,856 --> 00:19:12,496
What a beautiful young Grim Reaper sent to take me from this game.

109
00:19:16,036 --> 00:19:17,136
If you please.

110
00:19:17,996 --> 00:19:22,776
If someone was going to close the curtain on me, I couldn't have asked for anyone better.

111
00:19:23,176 --> 00:19:26,956
I thought I'd at least give one more good fight before fading away.

112
00:19:27,456 --> 00:19:29,536
And yet, even so,

113
00:19:31,116 --> 00:19:33,536
something inside of me broke free.

114
00:19:34,436 --> 00:19:35,836
I don't want to die.

115
00:19:35,836 --> 00:19:43,176
Here I was at the end of my career, ruining my legacy, struggling to keep up against a prodigy.

116
00:19:43,676 --> 00:19:46,116
A single thought welled up from within me.

117
00:19:46,756 --> 00:19:48,196
I don't want to lose.

118
00:19:48,456 --> 00:19:49,836
I don't want to lose.

119
00:19:50,156 --> 00:19:52,696
No matter what, I just don't want to lose.

120
00:19:53,056 --> 00:19:56,696
That was my crazed line of thought at the time.

121
00:19:56,696 --> 00:20:02,536
Mr. Matsunaga.

122
00:20:04,876 --> 00:20:07,036
Do you still love shogi?

123
00:20:07,036 --> 00:20:12,176
I don't know.

124
00:20:13,596 --> 00:20:15,036
How the hell would I know?

125
00:20:15,036 --> 00:20:26,056
When I'd win, I was so happy I wanted to shout with joy.

126
00:20:26,316 --> 00:20:30,756
But when I lost, it was agonizing, like someone stomping on me with muddy boots.

127
00:20:30,756 --> 00:20:35,116
I was tormented by the feeling that nobody wanted me to be part of this world.

128
00:20:36,836 --> 00:20:40,816
And yet, I just couldn't bring myself to quit.

129
00:20:43,596 --> 00:20:44,816
This feeling.

130
00:20:46,536 --> 00:20:50,796
How can I even begin to express the way I feel in words?

131
00:20:50,796 --> 00:21:07,856
Hello?

132
00:21:07,856 --> 00:21:07,996
Hello?

133
00:21:10,496 --> 00:21:12,036
Rey, where are you?

134
00:21:12,536 --> 00:21:16,236
I figured you might be depressed, so I thought I'd try to cheer you up.

135
00:21:16,936 --> 00:21:17,796
I heard.

136
00:21:18,216 --> 00:21:19,116
You won today.

137
00:21:19,116 --> 00:21:21,716
Oh well, it's win or lose after all.

138
00:21:22,796 --> 00:21:24,636
Just know it's not your fault.

139
00:21:25,316 --> 00:21:25,916
So...

140
00:21:25,916 --> 00:21:27,776
Mr. Matsunaga isn't quitting.

141
00:21:29,596 --> 00:21:31,796
He won't stop playing shogi.

142
00:21:33,876 --> 00:21:34,916
Hold on a minute.

143
00:21:35,316 --> 00:21:36,436
What does that even mean?

144
00:21:37,016 --> 00:21:37,316
Rey?

145
00:21:38,216 --> 00:21:38,776
Rey?

146
00:21:40,536 --> 00:21:42,396
Well, let's go.

147
00:21:42,736 --> 00:21:43,096
Okay.

148
00:21:43,536 --> 00:21:44,756
Come on, stand up.

149
00:21:49,116 --> 00:21:55,756
Hey, would you help me explain all of this to my wife and daughter?

150
00:21:56,296 --> 00:21:59,036
I've got to tell them that I've decided not to retire.

151
00:21:59,596 --> 00:22:01,436
They must be really worried about you.

152
00:22:02,316 --> 00:22:04,236
Shogi players do need physical strength.

153
00:22:04,236 --> 00:22:06,116
I don't ever want to quit.

154
00:22:07,236 --> 00:22:08,756
Because if I do...

155
00:22:08,756 --> 00:22:12,696
I won't be a big shot at home anymore.

156
00:22:14,756 --> 00:22:18,956
I've never helped with any of the housework saying that I needed to focus on Shogi.

157
00:22:19,236 --> 00:22:20,836
I certainly can't quit now.

158
00:22:20,976 --> 00:22:23,156
If I do, my family will destroy me.

159
00:22:23,156 --> 00:22:24,756
So that's why you're not quitting?

160
00:22:25,076 --> 00:22:27,536
My blood runs cold just thinking about it.

161
00:22:27,916 --> 00:22:28,156
Huh?

162
00:22:28,556 --> 00:22:28,956
Right.

163
00:22:29,196 --> 00:22:30,916
From now on, you're doing the housework.

164
00:22:31,076 --> 00:22:32,916
And I'll even train you how to do it.

165
00:22:33,616 --> 00:22:34,496
Hey, father.

166
00:22:34,796 --> 00:22:36,876
It's your turn to give your grandson a bath.

167
00:22:37,956 --> 00:22:38,816
Oh, the horror.

168
00:22:39,196 --> 00:22:42,096
They'll make me do dishes, laundry, and change my grandson.

169
00:22:42,436 --> 00:22:44,676
You should be happy to help out any way you can.

170
00:22:44,756 --> 00:22:45,656
It's only fair.

171
00:22:45,896 --> 00:22:46,936
I don't wanna...

172
00:22:46,936 --> 00:22:47,936
Don't say that.

173
00:22:48,156 --> 00:22:49,476
Families should help each other out.

174
00:22:49,856 --> 00:22:52,016
Do I have to teach you how to do housework now?

175
00:22:52,016 --> 00:22:53,416
I don't wanna...

176
00:22:53,416 --> 00:22:54,736
I don't wanna...

177
00:22:54,736 --> 00:22:58,616
No matter what anyone says, I don't wanna do it!

178
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:34,771
When did it start to hurt?

179
00:24:35,191 --> 00:24:38,111
When did Christmas become such a painful holiday for me?

180
00:24:38,731 --> 00:24:40,551
Dad, can we open them now?

181
00:24:41,091 --> 00:24:43,271
Whoa, it's a new game bomb!

182
00:24:43,491 --> 00:24:44,611
So what do you think, Ray?

183
00:24:44,751 --> 00:24:46,311
I love it, really, it's great!

184
00:24:46,831 --> 00:24:50,631
Which is better for a final Christmas memory, a winner or a loser?

185
00:24:51,911 --> 00:24:53,471
March comes in like a lion.

186
00:24:53,991 --> 00:24:55,511
You might not watch next time.

187
00:24:55,971 --> 00:24:56,691
Excuse me?

188
00:24:57,091 --> 00:24:57,871
That's crazy.

189
00:25:01,011 --> 00:25:30,991
Thank you.

